    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Triage social media comments with AI and approve replies in Slack\n\n### How it works\nFor brands and agencies that answer comments on Instagram, Facebook, TikTok, YouTube and Threads and want a person to check every reply. When a comment arrives, the workflow reads its thread in Rizamo, so OpenAI sees the conversation so far, and sorts it:\n\n- **Reply**: OpenAI drafts a short reply in the comment's language. Slack shows it with **Reply** and **Skip**, and Rizamo posts it only after a yes.\n- **Spam**: hidden on its network, which can be undone in Rizamo.\n- **Needs a person** (complaints, orders, anything sensitive): a Slack message tells the team.\n- **Nothing to say** (an emoji, a friend tagged): no reply.\n\nReplied, hidden and empty comments are then marked done, so Rizamo's inbox keeps only what a person still has to answer, skipped drafts included.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the verified community node `@rizamohq/n8n-nodes-rizamo` (tested with 0.1.1): open the nodes panel, search **Rizamo** and choose **Install** ([installation guide](https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/community-nodes/installation/verified-install/)).\n2. In Rizamo, open **Developers**, create an API key and add it in n8n as a **Rizamo API** credential.\n3. Connect OpenAI in **Sort the comment** and describe your brand at the end of its instructions.\n4. Connect Slack and pick a channel in **Ask for approval** and **Alert the team**.\n5. Activate the workflow. **New comment** creates its webhook in Rizamo, which needs an https address: n8n Cloud has one, and a self-hosted n8n needs a public one.\n\n### Customization\nPick profiles in **New comment** to cover one brand only. To have spam checked by a person too, connect the Spam output of **Route** to **Alert the team** instead of **Hide spam**.",
        "height": 720,
        "width": 520
      },
      "id": "f954993d-7b67-5289-8fdc-3b2c2cb5db7b",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
